d engineering." [Source]3. Foreign Language4. U.S. Government or HistoryNo credit given for U.S. Government or History because the qualifying course for the "History" section of "The Roots of the Modern Age" requirement is not a U.S. history survey. Furthermore, the qualifying course for the "Government" section of the "Roots of the Social Sciences" requirement is not an American government survey.6. Mathematics7. ScienceBWhat's on This Website?What Will They Learn?™ provides unique information on whether colleges make sure their students learn the things they need to know. You can find what they expect their graduates to study outside their majors, how much they[0m
